cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SpineSense: five-IMU garment-based trunk motion monitoring"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the dissertation it accompanies."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yikai
    family-names: Guo
    email: rmhkuox@ucl.ac.uk
    affiliation: "University College London"
abstract: >-
  Firmware and offline analysis pipeline for a five-IMU garment-based trunk
  motion monitoring system: I3C sensor bring-up with per-device dynamic
  addressing, body-chain orientation fusion, twist/bend decomposition,
  optical motion-capture alignment and empirical calibration, and movement
  classification over pre-segmented bouts. No human-subject data is included.
keywords:
  - inertial measurement unit
  - trunk motion
  - wearable sensing
  - sensor fusion
  - motion capture validation
  - rehabilitation engineering
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-03"
